  "reasoning": "The Labels type in prometheus (model/labels/labels_slicelabels.go) is defined as `type Labels []Label` — a sorted slice of Label structs. Changing this to a named struct with private fields and accessor methods would break all downstream repos that directly import `github.com/prometheus/prometheus/model/labels` and use Labels as a slice (iterating with range, indexing with [], constructing via slice literals, using len(), append(), etc.). Using Cypher queries against the code knowledge graph, I identified 6 repos (excluding prometheus itself) that have IMPORTS_EXTERNAL relationships to this package: mimir (79 files), loki (25 files), thanos (10 files), opentelemetry-operator (6 files), tempo (4 files), and opentelemetry-collector-contrib (1 file). Grafana was excluded because it only imports `github.com/prometheus/alertmanager/pkg/labels`, which is a separate package unaffected by this change."
